INSERT OR IGNORE INTO catalogue_pages (catalogue_id, page_num, text_content, char_count, has_extractable_text, search_text) VALUES ('24c796309c95d7fa', 140, '4500 Series - Electric Modifications
 FUNCTION # DESCRIPTION
 Request to Exit RX Used to shunt an alarm, activate an alarm, provide release of magnetic locks, or signal a console.
 Dual Request to Exit RX2 Features two SPDT switches
 Latchbolt Monitoring LM An internal SPDT switch that monitors the latchbolt to signal both egress and access of an opening.
 Latchbolt Monitoring/ RXLM Two internal SPDT switches that monitor the latchbolt and the pushbar simultaneously.
 Request to Exit
 Electric Trim ET Provides the means of locking or unlocking outside lever trim controls remotely. Trim works with both 12V
 or 24V and is field-selectable between Fail Safe (EL) or Fail Secure (EU).
 Authorized Ingress/Key AI An internal SPDT switch that monitors the operation of the outside trim. Must be ordered with the
 Monitoring device.
 Request to Exit/ RXAI Two internal SPDT switches that monitor the pushbar and the outside trim simultaneously. Must be
 Authorized Ingress ordered with the device.
 OnBoard Delayed OBDE Delays egress for 15 seconds (30 seconds optional) when unauthorized egress is initiated. Modification can
 Egress be made to 4501 exit devices.
 Delayed Egress DE Delays egress for 15 or 30 seconds when unauthorized egress is initiated. Wall mount controller (2-679-0630)
 provides digital countdown display with verbal instructions or alarm tone only and must be ordered separately.
 Motor Driven Electric MLR Provides the means of locking or unlocking exit devices remotely using an electric motor. Recommend Hager
 Latch Retraction 2903 or 2904 Power Supply.
 Motor Driven Electric MLRX Provides the means of locking or unlocking exit devices remotely using an electric motor, along with an
 Latch Retraction with SPDT switch. Recommend Hager 2903 or 2904 Power Supply.
 Request to Exit
 Motor Driven Electric MLRXLM Provides the means of locking or unlocking exit devices remotely using an electric motor along with two
 Latch Retraction with internal SPDT switches that monitor the pushbar and latchbolt simultaneously. Recommend Hager 2903 or
 Request to Exit and 2904 Power Supply.
 Latchbolt Monitoring
 Motor Driven Electric MLRLM Provides the means of locking or unlocking exit devices remotely using an electric motor along with an
 Latch Retraction with internal SPDT switch that monitors the latchbolt. Recommend Hager 2903 or 2904 Power Supply.
 Latchbolt Monitoring
 Electrified Mortise ELEU Provides the means of locking or unlocking outside lever trim controls remotely. Field selectable between
 Exit Device Fail Safe (EL) or Fail Secure (EU). Works with both 12V and 24V.


ELECTRICAL SPECIFICATION/RATINGS AND WIRE REQUIREMENTS
 Electrical • RX or LM; 125 VAC (3 AMP current); 30 VDC (2 AMP current)
 Specification/ • MLR; 1 AMP in rush @ 24 VDC +/- 2V, 400 mA holding
 Ratings: • DE; Single, 430 mA, Tandem 680 mA @ 24 VDC
 • OBDE; Single, 540 mA; Tandem 790 mA @ 24 VDC
 • ELEU; 12 or 24V, 250 mA Inrush, 10mA Holding

 Wire • Status switches (i.e. RX, LM, etc.) require 2 wires per switch to monitor a normally open (NO) or
 Requirements: normally closed (NC) position
 • All devices provide 3 wires per switch so both NO and NC positions can be monitored
 • Monitoring both positions will require 3 wires per switch


QUICK CONNECT
Available on AI, ED, LM, MLR, and RX

POWER SUPPLIES
For power supply options see electrified section.


 ALARMED DEVICES - SPECIFY WHEN ORDERING (Note: Alarm kit components may be purchased separately)
 ALK - Alarm Kit
 ALM - ALK with latch monitor switch (recommended for use with SVR devices)
 ALT - ALK with tamper switch
 ALL - ALK with latch monitor and tamper switch




20 2024 www.hagerco.com
