INSERT OR IGNORE INTO catalogue_pages (catalogue_id, page_num, text_content, char_count, has_extractable_text, search_text) VALUES ('24c796309c95d7fa', 162, '4600 Series - Electric Modifications
 FUNCTION # DESCRIPTION

 Request to Exit RX Used to shunt an alarm, activate an alarm, provide release of magnetic locks, or signal a console.

 Dual Request to Exit RX2 Features two SPDT switches

 Latchbolt Monitoring LM* An internal SPDT switch that monitors the latchbolt to signal both egress and access of an opening.
 Latchbolt Monitoring/ RXLM* Two internal SPDT switches that monitor the latchbolt and the pushbar simultaneously.
 Request to Exitt
 Delayed Egress DE Delays egress for 15 or 30 seconds when unauthorized egress is initiated. Wall mount controller (2-679-0630)
 provides digital countdown display with verbal instructions or alarm tone only and must be ordered separately.
 Motor Driven Electric MLR Provides the means of locking or unlocking exit devices remotely using an electric motor. Recommend Hager
 Latch Retraction 2903 or 2904 Power Supply.
 Motor Driven Electric MLRX Provides the means of locking or unlocking exit devices remotely using an electric motor, along with an
 Latch Retraction with SPDT switch. Recommend Hager 2903 or 2904 Power Supply.
 Request to Exit
 Motor Driven Electric MLRXLM* Provides the means of locking or unlocking exit devices remotely using an electric motor along with
 Latch Retraction with two internal SPDT switches that monitor the pushbar and latchbolt simultaneously. Recommend Hager
 Request to Exit and 2903 or 2904 Power Supply.
 Latchbolt Monitoring
 Motor Driven Electric MLRLM* Provides the means of locking or unlocking exit devices remotely using an electric motor along with an
 Latch Retraction with internal SPDT switch that monitors the latchbolt. Recommend Hager 2903 or 2904 Power Supply.
 Latchbolt Monitoring

 *Not available on the 4600 CVR or CLB.


 ELECTRICAL SPECIFICATION/RATINGS AND WIRE REQUIREMENTS
 Electrical • ED; .225 AMP @ 24 Volt +/- 2V
 Specifications/ • RX or LM; 125 VAC (3 AMP current); 30 VDC (2 AMP current)
 Ratings: • MLR; 1 AMP in rush @ 24 VDC +/- 2V, 400 mA holding

 Wire • Status switches (i.e. RX, LM, etc.) require 2 wires per switch to monitor a normally open (NO) or
 Requirements: normally closed (NC) position
 • All devices provide 3 wires per switch so both NO and NC positions can be monitored
 • Monitoring both positions will require 3 wires per switch


QUICK CONNECT
 Available on ED, LM, MLR, and RX

 POWER SUPPLIES
 PRODUCT # DESCRIPTION
 Provides 24 Volt DC power for Fail Safe or Fail Secure locking devices and interface with building alarm controls, card
 2903
 readers, keypads, and other door controls
 2904 Provides 24 Volt DC power and control for openings with an electrified locking device and automatic door operator
 2908 Provides up to 1 amp of 12 or 24 Volt DC power - modular
 2909 Provdes up to 2 amps of 12 or 24 Volt DC power - modular


