Selecting Degree of Hold Open or Stop
Overhead door holders and stops are designed to function effectively from 85º to 110º. The recommended minimum degree of
hold open would be set at 95° to put the door lever, pull, and panic hardware beyond the flow of traffic.

When selecting the degree of hold open for doors opening against a wall or back to back, there is approximately 5º to 7º of spring
engagement beyond the hold open or initial stop point, this is the dead stop.

For dead stop templating, the degree of opening should be set 5º to 7º less than the point of required dead stop to accommodate
the full compression of the shock absorber.




